[en.EVENT_CECIA_1]
Cassette Necklace - Changeling Empire Central Intelligence Agency Report

[en.EVENT_CECIA_1_desc]
The impression of Cozy Glow to most ponies is limited to her television image - the wings that declare power, the robe that displays authority, and the crown that exudes luxury. However, changeling intelligence operatives who infiltrated the Equestrian Royal Guard learned from the servants of the Empress that she often stares at a photo inside a cassette necklace at night. The photo must be of a pony that the Empress is very close to, but our operatives have not yet had the opportunity to see the true face of the pony in the photo.

[en.EVENT_CECIA_1_o0]
Emm...

[en.EVENT_CECIA_1_o1]
Damn, there are changeling spies among us!

[en.EVENT_CECIA_1_o2]
Fascinating Intel

[en.EVENT_CECIA_2]
Loyalist Medal - Changeling Empire Central Intelligence Agency Report

[en.EVENT_CECIA_2_desc]
Whenever Trixie is in front of the public, she always wears that loyalist medal - it was awarded to her by the Empress Cozy Glow as a “positive example of being previously misled but now reformed” during the coronation ceremony. But what’s interesting is that Trixie always wears it in a very inconspicuous place, as if she doesn’t want to be found. CECIA may be able to exploit this by contacting Trixie.

[en.EVENT_CECIA_2_o0]
Emm...

[en.EVENT_CECIA_2_o1]
Trixie does have a problem!

[en.EVENT_CECIA_2_o2]
Changeling’s conspiracy to trash Trixie!

[en.EVENT_CECIA_2_o3]
Oops, be careful next time

[en.EVENT_CECIA_2_o4]
Fascinating Intel

[en.EVENT_CECIA_3]
Brooch - Equestria Empire Ministry of Order Report

[en.EVENT_CECIA_3_desc]
Recently, we have intercepted an internal report from the Changeling Empire Central Intelligence Agency, the contents of which are as follows:
Trixie often wears a brooch produced in Saddle Arabia at public occasions. According to the changelings intelligence department, Trixie does not really appreciate this kind of jewelry herself, so this brooch is likely to have a special commemorative significance, but we are not sure if Trixie has any relationship with Saddle Arabia, perhaps we have got the focus of the investigation wrong.

[en.EVENT_CECIA_3_o0]
Okay

[en.EVENT_CECIA_3_o1]
Fascinating Intel

[en.EVENT_CECIA_3_o2]
Let them wonder then.

[en.EVENT_CECIA_3_o3]
Fascinating Intel

[en.EVENT_CECIA_4]
Grogal’s Bell - Changeling Empire Central Intelligence Agency Report

[en.EVENT_CECIA_4_desc]
The safety of Grogal’s Bell is always the top priority of the intelligence agencies of all countries. In the past year alone, there have been 13 attempts to steal or seize Grogal’s Bell, 6 of which were committed by unknown perpetrators. Lord Tirek has undoubtedly thwarted every conspiracy. CECIA has reflected on the details and causes of the previous 7 operations and has also considered the other 6 failed operations as a reference. CECIA has evaluated the success rate of Operation <=Thin Wing=> as: Low.

[en.EVENT_CECIA_4_o0]
Emm...

[en.EVENT_CECIA_4_o1]
Fascinating Intel

[en.EVENT_CECIA_4_o2]
Fascinating Intel

[en.EVENT_CECIA_5]
Pure Gold Helmet - Changeling Empire Central Intelligence Agency Report

[en.EVENT_CECIA_5_desc]
On the birthday celebration of Lord Tirek, his younger brother Scorpan gave him a pure gold helmet, which was majestic and prestigious. However, Tirek sneered at it and almost never wore the helmet in any public occasion. Scorpan has been trying to repair his relationship with his brother, but Tirek seems to be indifferent to it. With a little intervention, we may be able to use this to disrupt the stability within the centaur community.

[en.EVENT_CECIA_5_o0]
Emm...

[en.EVENT_CECIA_5_o1]
Fascinating Intel

[en.EVENT_CECIA_5_o2]
Fascinating Intel

[en.EVENT_CECIA_6]
Horn Badge - Changeling Empire Central Intelligence Agency Report

[en.EVENT_CECIA_6_desc]
During formal occasions of the Dragon Clan, Ember always wears a horn badge. This badge was given by Prince Rutherford, aiming to consolidate the generational friendship between the Yaks and the Dragons. However, in recent formal occasions, Ember did not wear this badge. CECIA speculates that this may be an expression of dissatisfaction with the recent rise of nationalism within the Yak tribe, which has led to the rejection of the Dragon Clan. With a little intervention, we may be able to worsen the relationship between the two sides.

[en.EVENT_CECIA_6_o0]
Emm...

[en.EVENT_CECIA_6_o1]
Fascinating Intel

[en.EVENT_CECIA_6_o2]
Fascinating Intel

[en.EVENT_CECIA_7]
Butterfly-shaped Cutie Mark - Changeling Empire Central Intelligence Agency Report

[en.EVENT_CECIA_7_desc]
Evidence shows that the Discord Legion is planning to collaborate with Starlight to launch an attack towards Canterlot. According to the intelligence sharing clause in the Canterlot Pact’s secret provisions, we are obligated to inform the Equestria Empire government... However, given the current tense political situation, CECIA suggests temporarily ignoring this intelligence and waiting for further observation.

[en.EVENT_CECIA_7_o0]
Emm...

[en.EVENT_CECIA_7_o1]
Fortunately we have spied on the Changelings

[en.EVENT_CECIA_7_o2]
Fascinating Intel

[en.EVENT_CECIA_8]
Crown - Changeling Empire Central Intelligence Agency Report

[en.EVENT_CECIA_8_desc]
§R<=TOP SECRET=>§!
Since Queen Chrysalis announced the establishment of the Changeling Empire Central Intelligence Agency, the development of the agency has been rapid, and has also received strong support from Queen Chrysalis. Now, CECIA’s antennae is spread all over the world, and it also has its own armed forces, which can execute various tasks throughout the entire Equestria.
However, what Queen Chrysalis did not realize is that the agency’s monitoring targets also include herself. “No one is above suspicion” - this is the core concept of CECIA. The secret group that collects intelligence about Queen Chrysalis reports directly to the Director of the agency - Trickster. The secret group is composed only of the Director’s confidants, and the outside world is almost unaware of the existence of this secret group.
What is worrying is that recent evidence suggests that our beloved Queen Chrysalis seems to be weaker, and her decisions are becoming more and more indecisive. The secret group speculates that this may be related to the corruption by “friendship”: as early as the time of the Ultimate Battle, the alliance between Queen Chrysalis and Warm Light Flow and Trickster has already surpassed a simple “cooperation” relationship and entered an inappropriate “friendship” range.
The secret group speculates that Queen Chrysalis has been delaying the approval of the Changeling Empire’s plan for a full-scale war against the pony race out of her friendship with Cozy Glow.
When required, the secret group believes that action should be taken to ensure that the future of the Changeling Empire and the Changeling race is not affected by “friendship”.

[en.EVENT_CECIA_8_o0]
Tacitly Consent

[en.EVENT_CECIA_8_o1]
What? Summon the Director of CECIA! Now!

[en.EVENT_CECIA_8_o2]
What? Execute the Director of CECIA!

[en.EVENT_CECIA_8_o3]
Fascinating Intel

[en.EVENT_CECIA_8_o4]
Fascinating Intel

[en.EVENT_CECIA_9]
The Hive Summon

[en.EVENT_CECIA_9_desc]
Summoned by Queen Chrysalis, The director of CECIA, Trickster, rushed from Hatchburg headquarter back to the Changeling Hive. He knew what the sudden and urgent summon from Queen Chrysalis meant — his secret group against Queen Chrysalis had been exposed. As soon as he entered the Hive, he saw the serious look from Queen Chrysalis and the emotionless standing guards. After a brief silence, Queen Chrysalis finally spoke.
First was anger, questioning and reprimanding Trickster’s loyalty. Trickster felt he couldn’t hear the specific reprimanding clearly anymore, he just looked at Queen Chrysalis quietly.
Then, Queen Chrysalis turned from anger to regret and sadness, talking about her support for CECIA, her nurturing and promotion of Trickster — from an ordinary soldier in the Hive, to a guard, to a captain, and then to the newly established CECIA’s director. But her kindness to Trickster seemed more like a sign of weakness in Trickster’s eyes.
When he was young, Trickster was already a loyal follower of Queen Chrysalis. After becoming a member of the guard, he could be in daily contact with Queen Chrysalis, listen to her teachings, and learn her thoughts. But these beautiful memories only belonged to the past — the Queen Chrysalis in front of him made Trickster feel strange.
Then, Queen Chrysalis seemed to calm down and began to list her actions, trying to persuade Trickster to believe in her “grand plan” for the Changeling race. She tried to persuade Trickster that the brief peace with the ponies was worth it. But as with the previous stages, Trickster did not intend to respond to this.
Next, Queen Chrysalis’s eyes were filled with disappointment. She ordered the guards to take Trickster away and imprison him in the Hive’s dungeon — rather than execute him. This finally eliminated the last hesitation in Trickster’s heart, and he knew his choice was correct.
Finally, Queen Chrysalis showed surprise — all the guards around her had been replaced by CECIA operatives. Of course, even though Queen Chrysalis had become weak, dealing with these operatives was not difficult, and Trickster clearly knew this.
Thus, at the very end, while Queen Chrysalis was furiously killing the operatives attacking her, Trickster calmly took out from his bag a specialized dark rock tailored against Queen Chrysalis, activated it, and put it on the ground. Then he took out a gas mask, slowly put it on, closed the door, and walked out of the Hive, leaving the chaos behind.

[en.EVENT_CECIA_9_o0]
Hail Trickster!

[en.EVENT_CECIA_10]
A Sad Day for the Changeling Empire

[en.EVENT_CECIA_10_desc]
Today, the Changeling Central Hive released a short but shocking news - the beloved Changeling Empire Queen, Chrysalis, died in the hive due to the infection of the swamp fever.
Queen Chrysalis had no husband nor heir. Before her death, she urgently summoned the Director of CECIA, Trickster, and entrusted him with the heavy responsibility of ruling the Changeling Empire.
After the death of Queen Chrysalis, Trickster held the inauguration ceremony and officially became the ruler of the Changeling Empire, promising to continue to implement the will of Queen Chrysalis and lead the Changeling race to a better future. Tonight, he will deliver his first speech at the funeral of Queen Chrysalis.
The sudden death of Queen Chrysalis has caused widespread concern in Equestria: Trickster has always been a loyal follower of Queen Chrysalis for a long time, and his radicalness is no less than that of Queen Chrysalis. It is understood that he has proposed three times for a full-scale war against ponies during his tenure as the Director of CECIA, all of which were shelved by Queen Chrysalis. Now, it seems that nothing can stop him anymore.

[en.EVENT_CECIA_10_o0]
Hail Trickster!

[en.EVENT_CECIA_10_o1]
Emm...

[en.EVENT_CECIA_11]
Universal Surveillance - Changeling Empire Central Intelligence Agency Report

[en.EVENT_CECIA_11_desc]
Evidence suggests that there still exists a very small number of unmetamorphosed changeling citizens who are dissatisfied with Queen Chrysalis, some of whom have infiltrated the upper echelons of changeling society, and there even exists assassination plans against Queen Chrysalis.
Although our beloved queen is powerful in magic, we cannot be complacent in the security of our great national leader. The Changeling Empire Central Intelligence Agency believes that the situation is urgent and requires immediate action.
CECIA proposes:
1. Establish a comprehensive surveillance system within the country to ensure the purity of thought of unmetamorphosed changelings. The surveillance targets not only citizens, but also the changeling army and the government’s upper echelons: “No one is above suspicion.”
2. The Queen’s Guard should undergo a strict re-screening to ensure that no rebels have infiltrated. At the same time, the Queen’s Guard should strengthen the protection of the queen to prevent any assassination attempts.
3. The Changeling Empire Central Intelligence Agency will launch a nationwide search for disloyal changelings to ensure the security of the country.
Due to the high cost of the above actions, we request financial support from the Changeling Empire. Out of concern for the queen’s safety, we request the queen’s approval as soon as possible.

[en.EVENT_CECIA_11_o0]
Approve

[en.EVENT_CECIA_11_o1]
Redundant, doubting my magical strength?

[en.EVENT_CECIA_11_o2]
Fascinating Intel

[en.EVENT_CECIA_11_o3]
Fascinating Intel

[en.EVENT_CECIA_12]
Dark Rock - Changeling Empire Central Intelligence Agency Report

[en.EVENT_CECIA_12_desc]
The Dark Rock is spread throughout the Changeling Empire. This ore has special magic that can weaken and shield the magic of non-changeling creatures. However, due to its high mining cost and the high demand for the magic to be activated and maintained, its application is relatively limited: currently only the throne of the Queen of the Chrysalis and a small number of elite changeling troops use it.
CECIA proposes to cooperate with the Defence Army and the Imperial War Science Research Institute to study the application of Dark Rock:
1. Reduce the cost of mining and subsequent use of Dark Rock, and strive to popularize the use of Dark Rock in the changeling army.
2. Dark Rock can only be used for defense at present, and research should be conducted to find its offensive applications.
3. Dark Rock is currently only effective against non-changeling creatures. It has no effect on suppressing the hatching of changelings and capturing internal rebel changelings. Specialized Dark Rock should be considered to deal with these situations.
According to the current draft of the research plan, only in the experimental stage, the expected amount of Dark Rock to be used is already three times the current total mining volume of the Empire. Therefore, promoting this plan will also help drive the development of the Empire’s mining industry.

[en.EVENT_CECIA_12_o0]
Approve

[en.EVENT_CECIA_12_o1]
Sounds a bit expensive

[en.EVENT_CECIA_12_o2]
Fascinating Intel

[en.EVENT_CECIA_12_o3]
Fascinating Intel

[en.EVENT_CECIA_13]
Biological Weapons - Changeling Empire Central Intelligence Agency Report

[en.EVENT_CECIA_13_desc]
CECIA’s antennae is spread all over the world, and the ree Equestria is one of our key targets: the Free Equestria is in contact with another world, a world inhabited by a creature called “human”.
It is understood that the creature “human” has rich experience in war, and their technological level far exceeds any species on the continent of Equestria. The Free Equestria is planning to introduce human war technology to the continent of Equestria.
In a rejected draft from the Free Equestria, our agents discovered a concept called “biological weapons”. The creature “human” believes that diseases can be used as weapons to indiscriminately attack enemy armies and civilians.
As good as the Changelings are at war and plunder, we have not previously even considered this method of warfare. The Free Equestria rejected the introduction of this technology on the grounds of “immorality”, but that does not mean that the Changelings should also reject it.
CECIA believes that this new concept of war is worth further study. We plan to conduct in-depth research on the prevalent infectious diseases on the continent of Equestria: Green Flu, Swamp Fever, Cutie Pox, Alicorn Flu, etc.
We will study the transmission routes, incubation periods, symptoms, treatment methods, and modification techniques of these diseases, so that we can use these diseases to strike the enemy when necessary. At the same time, we should also study the resistance of the Changeling species, so that we can protect ourselves when necessary.

[en.EVENT_CECIA_13_o0]
Approve

[en.EVENT_CECIA_13_o1]
That might be a little too extreme

[en.EVENT_CECIA_13_o2]
Fascinating Intel

[en.EVENT_CECIA_13_o3]
Fascinating Intel

[zh.EVENT_CECIA_1]
盒式项链坠——幻形灵帝国中央情报局报告

[zh.EVENT_CECIA_1_desc]
多数小马对于和煦光流女皇的印象停留在她的电视形象上——宣示力量的双翼，展现权威的皇袍，尽显奢华的皇冠。然而，打入小马利亚帝国亲卫队的幻形灵情报工作者在与服饰女皇的仆从交谈后得知，晚上常常能看到女皇盯着一个盒式项链坠里面的相片。照片上一定是女皇很亲近的小马，不过我们的情报人员至今还没有机会一睹照片中小马的真面目。

[zh.EVENT_CECIA_1_o0]
额...

[zh.EVENT_CECIA_1_o1]
可恶，我们之中有幻形灵间谍！

[zh.EVENT_CECIA_1_o2]
有趣的情报

[zh.EVENT_CECIA_2]
忠诚者勋章——幻形灵帝国中央情报局报告

[zh.EVENT_CECIA_2_desc]
每当特丽克西出现在公众面前时，她总是佩戴着那个忠诚者勋章——这是当年册封仪式上，和煦光流女皇将她做为“此前受到蛊惑，但已经洗心革面”的正面典型而为她颁发的。但耐马寻味的是，特丽克西总是将其佩戴在极其不显眼的地方，似乎不愿意被发现。情报局也许可以利用这一点，与特丽克西进行联系。

[zh.EVENT_CECIA_2_o0]
额...

[zh.EVENT_CECIA_2_o1]
特丽克西果然有问题！

[zh.EVENT_CECIA_2_o2]
可能是幻形灵的离间计！

[zh.EVENT_CECIA_2_o3]
糟糕，下次注意

[zh.EVENT_CECIA_2_o4]
有趣的情报

[zh.EVENT_CECIA_3]
胸针——小马利亚帝国秩序部报告

[zh.EVENT_CECIA_3_desc]
近日，我们截获了幻形灵中央情报局内部的一封报告，内容如下：
特丽克西在出席公众场合时，常常佩戴一只产于鞍拉伯的胸针。据幻形灵情报部门，特丽克西平日并不喜欢这类首饰，因此这枚胸针很可能具有特殊的纪念意义，但我们尚不清楚特丽克西与鞍拉伯有任何关系，或许是我们搞错了调查的重点。

[zh.EVENT_CECIA_3_o0]
好吧

[zh.EVENT_CECIA_3_o1]
有趣的情报

[zh.EVENT_CECIA_3_o2]
让他们想破脑袋去吧。

[zh.EVENT_CECIA_3_o3]
有趣的情报

[zh.EVENT_CECIA_4]
格罗迦之铃——幻形灵帝国中央情报局报告

[zh.EVENT_CECIA_4_desc]
格罗迦之铃的安全永远是各国情报部局的首要任务。仅在过去一年就发生了13起试图偷窃或抢夺格罗迦之铃的行为，其中6起作案者不明。提雷克大王毫无悬念地挫败了每一起阴谋。幻形灵中央情报局反思了此前7次行动细节和失败原因，并参考了另外6起的失败原因分析，情报局评估「薄翼」行动的成功率为：低。

[zh.EVENT_CECIA_4_o0]
额...

[zh.EVENT_CECIA_4_o1]
有趣的情报

[zh.EVENT_CECIA_4_o2]
有趣的情报

[zh.EVENT_CECIA_5]
纯金头盔——幻形灵帝国中央情报局报告

[zh.EVENT_CECIA_5_desc]
在提雷克大王的生日庆典上，提雷克的弟弟斯科潘送给了提雷克一个纯金的头盔，威严显赫。然而，提雷克对此嗤之以鼻，几乎从未在任何公众场合穿戴过这一头盔。斯科潘一直以来试图修复与哥哥的关系，但提雷克似乎对此毫无兴趣。稍加干预，我们也许可以借此破坏半人马族群内部的稳定。

[zh.EVENT_CECIA_5_o0]
额...

[zh.EVENT_CECIA_5_o1]
有趣的情报

[zh.EVENT_CECIA_5_o2]
有趣的情报

[zh.EVENT_CECIA_6]
号角徽章——幻形灵帝国中央情报局报告

[zh.EVENT_CECIA_6_desc]
在龙族的正式场合，余焰总是会佩戴一个号角徽章。这一徽章是卢瑟福公子赠送的，意在巩固牦牛与龙族的世代友好。但近日多次正式场合中，余焰并未佩戴这一徽章。情报局推测这可能是在表达对于今日牦牛氏族内部民族主义抬头，排斥龙族的若干事件的不满。稍加干预，我们也许可以恶化双方的关系。

[zh.EVENT_CECIA_6_o0]
额...

